Description: SecureEye face authentication for Linux
 SecureEye authenticates Linux users with their face. This package ships the
 complete stack: the C/C++ PAM module, the secureeye-authd authentication
 daemon it talks to over a UNIX socket, the Python recognition runtime and the
 secureEye command line tool.
 .
 Recognition backends come from the distribution rather than a bundled
 virtualenv: python3-mediapipe (amd64 only) is the default backend and
 python3-dlib is the alternative, selectable via detector_backend in
 /etc/secureEye/config.ini. On architectures without mediapipe, set
 detector_backend = dlib.
